@startuml poll-interval
' cumin works - the poll interval of a repository: every poll interval when in work, the idle poll interval otherwise.
' Document: poll.md, section on the poll interval.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif

start
repeat
  :tick of poll_interval;
  :read the stop request;
  while (next target repository?) is (yes)
    if (in work, or idle_poll_interval over\nsince the last poll, or stop after the runs?) then (yes)
      :poll the repository:
      read the snapshot, decide, apply;
      :keep the time of the poll,
      its result, and whether
      an issue is in work;
    else (no)
      :skip the repository:
      no GitHub call;
    endif
  endwhile (no)
repeat while (stop?) is (no)
->yes;
stop

note right
  In work, one of:
  * no poll of the repository ran yet
  * the last poll failed
  * the last poll took an action
  * an agent run of the repository is in progress,
    or one ended since the last poll
  * an open requirement issue has
    cumin/status/ready or planning
  * an open sub-issue has cumin/status/ready,
    implementing, checking, or reviewing
  * an open requirement issue has
    cumin/status/awaiting-plan-review and
    one or more sub-issues, all closed
end note
@enduml
